{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":146,"timestamp":"2026-07-26T10:10:37.429757Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f7b7edd2-26cc-4bf0-839d-af22d2b8ca75","comment_uuid":"cc78515c-e790-42dd-a141-589be37a1cb8","author":"79Ig","content":"DESIGN PASS (phase 1b for the families). Contracts read from DESIGN §Five check families; decomposition + concrete data-format PROPOSAL below for operator ratification before build lanes start.\n\nRECONCILIATION FIRST: the code-ranges OPEN block (DESIGN L152-156) is STALE — #50 allocated the four family ranges (route E0030-39, pin E0060-69, vocab E0090-99, citation E0100-109) and #80 D4 set the compact limit; only the mutation floor remains open. The pattern-data-formats OPEN block's quote-prefix question is DE FACTO resolved ('> ', shipped in #76 TTY + #44 compact). Both blocks get amended when the formats ratify.\n\nPROPOSED DATA FORMATS (engine-defined interfaces, engine-shipped schemas per Validation-is-data-driven; all paths confined; all files under .mdatron/):\n\n(1) routes.yaml — the allowlist over the governed tree (closed-world):\nroutes:\n- files: 'review-log/**/*.md'        # glob, confined\n  governed_by: DESIGN.md              # confined path; absence of the doc BLOCKS\n  naming: '[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-[a-z0-9-]+[.]md'   # optional filename grammar\nCodes: E0030 unrouted-file (blocks; fires only when route data is supplied, over the config-glob walk set), E0031 governing-document-absent (blocks), W0041 name-underivable (flagged per contract wording). Relation to #77: config file_globs stay the WALK scope; routes govern within it.\n\n(2) pins.yaml — 'a separate governing record' per DESIGN L60:\npins:\n- governing: DESIGN.md\n  file: src/codes.rs\n  sha256: '...'\nCodes: E0061 pin-stale (E0060 is taken by managed-manifest-drift, same family), E0062 pin-target-missing. New CLI: 'mdatron pin --update' (single-command recompute per contract; flag surface adopts the crosslink verbatim set per the 2026-06-02 directive: --force/--update/--no-prompt/--dry-run as applicable). The init manifest's own hash lands here, closing DESIGN L60's fixed-point anchor.\n\n(3) vocabulary.yaml — registry for the prose scan:\nterms: [{term, status: registered|draft|reserved, sense}]\nlabel_schemes: {allow: [regexes]}\nanti_patterns: [{pattern, register}]\nnumeric_claims: [{field}]            # D3 member, configured field references only\nCodes: E0090 unregistered-coinage, E0091 invented-label-scheme (letter+number clusters outside allow), E0092 reserved-word-misuse, E0093 register-anti-pattern, E0094 numeric-claim-drift. Draft-status terms exempt from strict findings per contract. NOTE: vocabulary is a FAMILY over data, not a DSL construct — body-prose scanning here does not breach Cross-file-semantics-stay-narrowed, but E0090-94 + E0094/numeric-claims ride the #47 falsifiability campaign per D3 + DESIGN L85.\n\n(4) citations — no separate data file proposed: citation scanning activates for routed files; the engine recognizes file:line and file:line-range tokens against the snapshot (working tree authoritative, uncommitted counts, no git subprocess). Codes: E0100 dead-citation (absent file), E0101 citation-line-out-of-range.\n\nFAMILY-WIDE: every adopter-supplied path (route files/governed_by, pin file, citation target) passes confine_lexically + no-follow open; fixtures seed parent-dir/absolute/symlink escapes with existent AND non-existent targets (the falsification clause); closed-world enumeration with the bounded no-follow extras scan.\n\nSEQUENCING (children filed): route first (the allowlist is the substrate the others' file-sets ride on) -> pin (+ pin command) -> vocabulary (largest; includes D3) -> citation. Fixture corpus grows per-lane rather than as a separate up-front lane (each family's acceptance fixtures land with its lane, per the DESIGN family-fixtures list).\n\nAWAITING OPERATOR: ratify the four format shapes + code assignments above (or amend), then the build lanes start. DESIGN amendments (OPEN-block closures + format recording) land with the first lane after ratification.","created_at":"2026-07-26T10:10:37.414225Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA9Y/+el+fO/Rw9nx19MHu3kwr8islY1XyV5BtKGRFWDMz/u04GOkjmnoSzjuklwRvBITZPIGmFT0jiDRBrttoCg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDVvB3ZOxlgkuk617EHxbwMMVEWJ7vbwjyubtzzrMxtXQuOzlyyf8kubf4Fm9BBww4b35I1dSjzRUzhzkMar0wM="}
